maria_docs: I opened a docs PR that combines a short pricing-calculator example, a clarification to the rate-limits table, and two SDK snippets (old header -> new usage header migration). PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4507 :seedling:
thomas_prod: nice. can you paste the calculator example and the SDK snippet here? I want to make sure the pricing numbers align with the latest pricing grid (we bumped burst unit price last sprint).
eli_eng: quick infra note: embeddings cost is metered separately (per-embed unit) and doesn't count against token-based quotas; worth clarifying in the examples so folks don't double-count.
maria_docs: pasted below. kept it compact.

Pricing calculator (compact example, JS):
```js
// estimate monthly cost for text gen heavy workload
const tokensPerRequest = 1200;
const requestsPerDay = 50_000;
const daysPerMonth = 30;

const monthlyTokens = tokensPerRequest * requestsPerDay * daysPerMonth;
// pricePerToken comes from pricing table (USD per 1k tokens)
const pricePer1k = 0.0065; // updated grid (confirm)
const monthlyCost = (monthlyTokens / 1000) * pricePer1k;
console.log(`~$${monthlyCost.toFixed(2)}/mo`);
```

SDK header migration snippet (curl + JS):
```bash
# old header
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "X-Redwood-Rate: 1000" https://api.redwood.ai/v1/usage

# new header
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" -H "X-Redwood-Usage-Limit: 1000" https://api.redwood.ai/v1/usage
```

```js
// JS SDK old -> new header helper
function migrateHeaders(h) {
  if (h['X-Redwood-Rate']) {
    h['X-Redwood-Usage-Limit'] = h['X-Redwood-Rate'];
    delete h['X-Redwood-Rate'];
  }
  return h;
}
```

maria_docs: I also added a short paragraph about quota edge cases: when customers use embeddings + text-gen in same project they should inspect meter tags (unit=embed vs unit=token) to avoid double-billing in internal reports.
eli_eng: please call out the metric name for embedding units (redwood.embedding_units) and show a PromQL snippet for a combined view.
maria_docs: adding that now. PromQL example:
```promql
sum(rate(redwood_embedding_units_total{project="proj_xyz"}[5m]))
+ sum(rate(redwood_rate_limit{project="proj_xyz"}[5m]))
```

maria_docs: two housekeeping items: 1) fixed two broken links to the dashboard panels (old path /dashboards/quota -> /dashboards/usage-quota) and 2) added a redirect note so the legacy link still resolves for 14 days.
thomas_prod: nit: for the calculator example can we show an embeddings add-on line item (e.g., 2M embeds @ $0.0004 each) so product folks can eyeball combined cost?
maria_docs: good idea, added an embeddings row and a short table in prose. also added a short sample TypeScript typing for the SDK snippet per kevin's previous request.

TypeScript snippet (headers helper):
```ts
type Headers = Record<string, string>;
function migrateHeaders(h: Headers): Headers {
  if ('X-Redwood-Rate' in h) {
    return {...h, 'X-Redwood-Usage-Limit': h['X-Redwood-Rate']};
  }
  return h;
}
```

